  "query_preview": "(Thursday through Sunday)...\nOn Thursday, A low pressure system moving toward the California\ncoast will weaken high pressure aloft with lower-level flow \nbecoming onshore and strengthening. High temperatures on Thursday \nwill cool a few degrees for the deserts to around 5 degrees for \nthe coast into the valleys. High temperatures on Thursday for the\ncoast and valleys will be mostly in the mid 70s to mid 80s with \nthe warmest high temperatures, in the lower to mid 80s, for \ninland coastal areas into the western valleys.\n\nThat low pressure system approaching the California coast on\nThursday has both model timing and track differences as it moves\ntoward the southeast, and then inland across northern and central\nBaja on Friday and Friday night. This will bring additional\ncooling for Friday and Saturday with high temperatures on Saturday\nfor the coast and valleys mostly in the 70s, in the lower deserts\naround 80, and for the mountains in the 50s and 60s. This will \nalso bring a chance of showers with uncertain timing for some time\nfor Friday into Saturday. The greater amounts are expected\nsomewhere across central Baja with lighter rainfall possibly \nextending into portions of southwestern California.\n\nAdditional low pressure systems could bring precipitation at times\nfor late in the weekend into next week, but with even greater \ntiming and track differences.",
